 "part_mesh_sha256": "ca20c0fa61e6d3ce7b04bed25360e048e31dfd88ace04187aa6d9e8f4ca3fd0f",
 "about": "Robotiq 2F-85 at full opening: mujoco_menagerie f3b6013, robotiq_2f85/2f85.xml (BSD-2-Clause, ROS-Industrial; derived from ros-industrial/robotiq's robotiq_2f_85_gripper_visualization): every joint at 0, each driver at the open end of its range 0..0.8 rad, the silicone pads' faces 85.400 mm apart.  The bodies are base_mount.stl and base.stl and, on each finger's four-bar linkage, driver.stl, coupler.stl, spring_link.stl, follower.stl and pad.stl (the fingertip's plate under the silicone pad), where 2f85.xml places them; the Library mesh is the right finger's silicone_pad.stl, the pad the gripper grips with.  The other finger is 2f85.xml's left one: the same links turned 180 degrees about the gripper's axis (its quat 0 0 0 1), so its sensor is the same board.  The looks: drawn after Robotiq's studio photos of the 2F-85 (robotiq.com, the 2F-85 and 2F-140 product page: 2F_Adaptive_Grippers_White.png, the open grippers side by side; 2F-84 2F-140 montage.png, seen from below), 2026-11-16: the satin black anodised housing and coupling, the bead-blasted aluminium palm block between the fingers with its screws, the black anodised links of each finger's four-bar linkage (the inner link, spring_link.stl, and the outer one, coupler.stl), the aluminium driver inside them, the bright machined aluminium fingertip (follower.stl and the pad's plate, pad.stl) and the black silicone pad (the Library's part).  The pins' heads in the outer links' pivots and the cap and pin of the inner link's bore are the project's own drawing, plain cylinders (bodies/robotiq-2f-85/drawn-coupler-pins.stl, drawn-spring-link-pins.stl and drawn-spring-link-caps.stl), where the model leaves the holes open; the inner link's far pins are the model's own.  Not modelled: the ROBOTIQ lettering, the coupling's status light, the screws of the links' faces.",
